## How each discipline folder is organized

```
<discipline>/
  README.md     scope + curated links + index of what is here
  learned/      durable understanding (concepts, techniques, limits)
  configs/      tool configuration with rationale
  runbooks/     repeatable procedures
  findings/     dated observations
```

`learned/` holds understanding; `findings/` holds evidence. Do not mix them. `findings/` stays
empty until there is hardware to observe.

## Conventions

- Timestamps in UTC; location as city or grid square only.
- Cite upstream sources; mark version-dependent steps "verify before running".
- No secrets, credentials, or precise private locations.
- Cross-link back to the device documentation in [`../docs/`](../docs/).

